  "notes": "Atlanta girl group across three boards — an NJS debut, Dallas Austin's jazzier sample-soul, then She'kspere's jittery post-Timbaland R&B, 1991–2002. The research gives \"BPM 86–106 straight; ballads 73–93\", so the band runs 73–106 straight with the mode at 94, the tempo of the sourced \"Creep\" reading. The drum deltas come from the FanMail description — \"stop-start and insectile — gated, gapped 16ths with silence used as a hit\" — which is why `hihat.continuous` is false, `beatSkipProb` is authored and the kick's secondary anchor moves to the 16th before 3 (`2a`) rather than the genre's 8th; `syncopation` is pushed above the parent because the kick and snare are described as landing on unexpected 16ths. Harmony is the plucked two-chord vamp the entry describes (\"a Kurzweil acoustic-guitar patch\", a \"late-night trumpet sample plus jiggling funk guitar\"), with one diatonic major family for the sourced G-major cut. \"Narrow-interval unison-plus-third stacks, not wide gospel spreads\" is encoded as a low leap share, a low octave-jump probability and a 3–5 pitch motif. ⚠ The INFERRED parameters are `swing.amount` 0.58, every velocity and density number, and the bass settings — the debut's swung 16ths are marked `[LOW-CONF, genre-level]` in the research and a \"thin, dry sub\" is a mix direction, read here as a root-locked mirror-kick line with almost no glide.",
